Vortex Ring State
oVortices pile up on each other and form a
torus shaped ring due to air from bottom
oRing grows and bursts periodically
oCauses loss of thrust on rotor
(sometimes leading to accidents)
oUnsteady flow
oAnalytical analysis difficult. Rely on
empirical predictions


Turbulent Wake State
oRotor behaves like a bluff body
oFlow unsteady, rely on empirical means


